    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid Insurance Certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A copy of the bike’s insurance policy should show that coverage is active up to the date of departure. The certificate must include the policy number, coverage period, and the insurer’s contact details.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA‑Approved Consignment Bilty:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The Indian Bill of Lading (IBA) consignment bilty is the official transport document that confirms the consignor, consignee, and freight details. It must be signed by the consignor and the carrier, and retained by both parties.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Among these documents, the <strong>100% Declared‑Value Marine Transit Insurance</strong> stands out as a critical safeguard.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This insurance covers the full declared value of the motorcycle against loss, damage, or theft during maritime transit.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>By opting for a 100% coverage policy, you eliminate the risk of under‑insurance, ensuring that the entire value of the bike is protected regardless of the circumstances.</span></li></ul>
<p>The insurer will require proof of the bike’s market value, which can be verified through a recent appraisal or a dealer’s invoice. Once the policy is in force, the insurance certificate should be attached to the consignment bilty and kept with the RC and PUC copies for quick reference during inspection.</p>

<p>It is advisable to verify each document’s validity with the relevant authorities before the bike’s departure. Keep digital copies in a secure cloud storage, and carry physical originals for any on‑the‑road checks. By following this checklist, you can transport your motorcycle to Nuzvid with confidence, knowing that all regulatory and safety requirements are fully met.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



